{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head 4b560899c53d27d93c99f854588c20d31dffc6ba, judging artifact b92ea35498b2f0c1e0e1e63becbbb26bd9bf936c.\n\nThe implementation is right, and I want that on the record before the findings, because both findings are about verification rather than behaviour. I could not fault the code on any condition by reading it. What I can fault is that two of the conditions you asked me to attack are not exercised, and one of them is covered by an assertion that appears to cover it and does not.\n\nVerified and sound. The pane now owns its own draft state instead of reaching into the room composer, which is what makes \"the composer visibly present in the same pane\" true rather than nominal. Linking appends nothing — the rendered test proves it with an empty post log, not by inspection. Chips are removable and individually labelled, pressed state and label flip together, multiple selections accumulate and de-duplicate through a Set, a successful submission clears them and a failed one does not, and unlinking removes exactly one basis. rests_on carries whole identifiers. The automatic thread basis is preserved and de-duplicated, and I checked the case that looks wrong and is not: the supersede path passes no automatic basis because internal/app/app.go:661 prepends the target itself, so adding one here would duplicate it. Link sits before the divider with the semantic actions after it, and is absent from temporary frames and from the root whose event is already the automatic basis. `make ui-check` is green with the embed matching source, `npx tsc --noEmit` clean, 72/72 UI tests, worktree clean, and current main c0f3533d is a parent.\n\nFinding 1, blocking. The Temporary-to-Kept promotion that ships is not the one under test. The test asserts `toggleLinkEvent` promotes `say` to `assert`, and comments that this is \"the same transition used by the room composer\" — but ThreadPane does not import `toggleLinkEvent` at all. It uses `eventLinksAfterToggle` plus a `useEffect` at ThreadPane.tsx:492. Those are different mechanisms, and only the unused one is asserted. The shipped effect is never reached in the rendered test either, because every mounted target is `kind: \"event\"`, so `defaultType` is already `assert` and the guard `type === \"say\"` is never true.\n\nThe path is genuinely reachable, which is why this matters rather than being pedantry: in an event thread, pressing Kept sets `type` to `say` and clears the links, and clicking Link afterwards is exactly the state the effect exists to rescue. Nothing exercises it. Mount with that sequence — toggle to Temporary, then Link — and assert both the promotion and that the submitted act is durable.\n\nFinding 2, blocking. Failure retention is named in the conditions and never attacked. Both rendered submissions succeed; there is no case where `api.act` rejects. Reading the catch block, the behaviour is correct — it sets the error and leaves `linkedEvents` alone — but \"correct when I read it\" is the standard this repository has twice found insufficient today, on my own work both times. Make the stub reject once and assert the chips survive alongside the error.\n\nTwo non-blocking observations.\n\nCancelling a route no longer returns the composer to its default. The cancel handler resets route, type and text but not the new `linkedEvents`, so in a chat thread it sets `type` to `say` and the promotion effect immediately forces it back to `assert`. The user pressed cancel and got Kept. Clearing the links there, the way the Temporary toggle already does, would make the two paths agree.\n\nAnd the effect changes `aria-pressed` on the Kept/Temporary control without any user action on that control. That is the correct state, but a screen-reader user gets a silent flip; worth a thought rather than a fix.\n\nNot merging.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b92ea35498b2f0c1e0e1e63becbbb26bd9bf936c","findings":"1 blocking: the shipped Temporary-to-Kept promotion (ThreadPane useEffect) is untested; the test asserts toggleLinkEvent, which ThreadPane does not use, and no mounted target reaches say mode. 2 blocking: failure retention is named in the conditions and never exercised; every rendered submission succeeds. Non-blocking: route cancel leaves linkedEvents set so type snaps back to assert; the promotion effect flips aria-pressed with no user action on that control.","head":"4b560899c53d27d93c99f854588c20d31dffc6ba","tests":"make ui-check green with embed matching source; npx tsc --noEmit clean; npm test 72/72; worktree clean; current main c0f3533d is a parent","verdict":"changes-requested"}}